window.HELP_SEARCH=[{"id":"welcome","title":"What is Raap Nexus","summary":"A private AI workspace that answers from your own systems, builds dashboards and runs approvals and automations on your computer.","text":"The idea in one minute Raap Nexus runs on your computer. You ask a question in plain words, and an AI agent looks the answer up in your systems (your ERP, a database, a folder of files) and writes it back, often with a table or a chart. Anything worth keeping can be pinned to a dashboard that refreshes by itself. What you can do with it You want to Where Ask questions about your business data Chat Keep the answers in front of you Dashboards Run a task every morning, or ask someone to approve a request Automations and Approvals Make sure the AI follows your rules Guardrails and Mask personal details Let customers get answers on WhatsApp or Instagram Customer channels Give your team their own sign-ins and limits Users and permissions How your data is treated Your data stays on this computer. The app, its database and your settings live in a data folder on your machine, encrypted and tied to it. Read-only by default. Connectors only read. A tool that could create, change or delete something stops and asks you to Allow or Deny first (read more). You choose the AI. Use an AI command-line tool already installed on your computer (Claude, Codex, Gemini, Ollama and others), or any model reachable by a web address and key. Raap Nexus is developed by Techlogica IT DT Solutions PVT LTD. You can use it without registering; registering unlocks more connectors, plans and updates (Register with Techlogica)."},{"id":"install","title":"Install Raap Nexus","summary":"Windows installer, macOS package, running from source on any system, and the Android app. No admin rights are needed on Windows.","text":"Before you start A computer running Windows 10 or 11 (64-bit), macOS 11 or newer, or Linux. At least one way to reach an AI model: an AI command-line tool that is signed in on this computer, or a model address and key. You can set this up after installing (AI agents). Windows Download the installer, RaapNexus-Setup-<version>.exe , from Techlogica. Double-click it. It installs for your user only, so it needs no administrator rights, and it brings its own Python runtime. Choose whether to add a desktop shortcut and whether to start when I sign in . Keep that option on if you use schedules (Automations) because they only run while Raap Nexus is running. Finish. Raap Nexus opens in your browser at http://localhost:8787 . The installer is not code-signed yet, so Windows may show an unknown-publisher message. If you downloaded it from Techlogica, choose More info and then Run anyway . macOS Download RaapNexus-<version>-mac.zip and unzip it. Right-click Install Raap Nexus.command and choose Open . It copies Raap Nexus.app to Applications. Open the app. It needs Python 3.9 or newer and tells you if it is missing. The package is not signed by Apple, which is why you right-click the first time. A READ ME FIRST file inside the zip explains the same. Any system, from source You only need Python 3.9 or newer (no extra packages, no build step). System Start it with Windows double-click start.bat macOS and Linux ./start.sh Anywhere python raapnexus.py Useful options: --port 9000 , --host 0.0.0.0 (reachable from your network, off by default), --data <folder> , --no-browser . Run python raapnexus.py stop to stop it. Android The Android app is a window onto the copy of Raap Nexus that runs on your computer. Install the .apk from Techlogica, then give it your computer's address (Use it on your phone). Where your data lives Installed copies keep your data outside the program folder, so updates and reinstalls never touch it: %APPDATA%\\Raap Nexus on Windows and ~/Library/Application Support/Raap Nexus on macOS. The uninstaller asks before it touches your data. Opening Raap Nexus again while it is running just opens the running copy. To stop it, use Stop Raap Nexus in the Start menu (Windows) or python raapnexus.py stop ."},{"id":"first-run","title":"Create your workspace and sign in","summary":"The first visit creates the owner login. Then you pick your language, finish the Get started list and save your recovery code.","text":"Create the owner login The very first time you open Raap Nexus it asks you to create the login for this workspace. Open http://localhost:8787 (the installer does this for you). Choose your language from the list at the top of the card. All 18 languages are available (Languages and appearance). Type a Username , a Password and the same password again, then press Create account & start. The person who creates the first login is the owner : every permission, always. The owner adds everyone else later (Users and permissions). The owner login cannot be recovered by email. Choose a strong password you will remember, and save the recovery code described below. Get started A short checklist waits on the chat screen: connect your data, choose an AI agent, ask your first question, and keep it in front of you (a dashboard). Each step ticks itself when you do it. Press Hide this when you no longer need it. Save your recovery code Raap Nexus encrypts its data and ties it to this computer. If you ever move to a new computer or change hardware, the recovery code is what lets you open your data again. The first time you sign in, a red banner reminds you. Open Settings > System > Data protection and press Show my recovery code, then print it or write it down and keep it away from this computer (Data protection and sign-in security). Signing in later Use the same address and your username and password. If your administrator turned on a second step, you also type a 6-digit code from your authenticator app."},{"id":"tour","title":"A tour of the screen","summary":"The sidebar, the chat box and where each setting lives.","text":"The sidebar Item What it does New chat Starts a fresh conversation. Your dashboards One entry per dashboard you may see. Open it to see its tabs and widgets (Dashboards). Automations Workflows, templates, approvals and alerts (Automations). Settings Everything you configure, in six groups: AI, Data, Customers, People, System and Account. Search chats Finds an earlier conversation. Your chats are listed by day below it. At the bottom of the sidebar, from the left: your name, Phone mode , the language button, dark or light , and sign out . The small button at the top collapses the sidebar. The chat box Below the question field you choose what the question is about and who answers it: Dashboard : the dashboard this chat is about. Only that dashboard's connectors are used, and widgets are added to it. Connectors : shows how many connectors the chat can reach. Team: lets the lead model split work across your other agents (Team mode). Model : the agent and model that answers. The microphone for voice typing, and the send arrow. Type / to pick a skill for a single message (Skills in chat). Settings at a glance Group Pages AI Agents & models, Skills, Guardrails, Agent history Data Connectors, Dashboards Customers Channels (WhatsApp and Instagram) People Users and permissions System Domain & port, General, Health & support, Data protection, Techlogica, Version history Account My account, Notifications You only see the pages you have permission for."},{"id":"language","title":"Languages and appearance","summary":"18 interface languages, light and dark themes and an accent colour, chosen per browser.","text":"Choose a language Raap Nexus speaks 18 languages: English, Arabic, Urdu, French, German, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese (Brazil), Russian, Turkish, Hindi, Telugu, Tamil, Malayalam, Indonesian, Chinese (Simplified), Japanese and Korean. Arabic and Urdu mirror the whole layout from right to left. On the sign-in screen use the language list at the top of the card, or click the globe button at the bottom of the sidebar, or open Settings > System > General and use Language. The choice is saved in this browser. Each person, and each browser, can use a different language. Texts without a translation yet stay in English, and translations are machine-quality until a native speaker has reviewed them. Theme and accent colour Under Settings > System > General > Appearance choose System, Light or Dark, and one of four accent colours. The moon button in the sidebar switches quickly. This help centre The language list at the top of every help page changes the text, the screenshots and the button names to match your language. The translations are machine-made and not yet reviewed by a native speaker; the English text is the reference."},{"id":"agents-overview","title":"AI agents and models","summary":"An agent is any AI you want to work with: a CLI on this computer, or any model reachable by a web address and key.","text":"What an agent is Raap Nexus does not have an AI of its own. It lets you plug in the AIs you already use. Every one of them is called an agent , and there are two kinds: CLI agents are AI command-line tools installed and signed in on this computer: Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, Ollama, Cursor and others. There are no API keys to paste. URL agents are any model reachable by a web address with a key: OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter, Groq or a local server. The agent list Open Settings > AI > Agents & models. Each agent has a card with a switch, Test , Sign in (for CLIs that need it) and an edit button. Switch on the ones you want: the model picker in the chat and Team mode use whichever are on. Agent Can use your connectors Notes Claude Code Yes Install it, run claude once in a terminal and sign in. Codex CLI Yes Install it (or the Codex desktop app), then run codex login . Models are read from Codex itself. Gemini CLI Yes Needs an API key (Google AI Studio) or Vertex credentials under Edit > Environment. Ollama (local models) No, text only Local, private and free. Pull a model first, for example ollama pull llama3.2 . Cursor Agent and others No, text only Experimental adapters. Your own CLI or URL model Optional See the next two articles. Install a CLI for me If a CLI is missing, its card shows Install for me . You first see exactly what will run and where it comes from, and you must confirm before anything is downloaded. Which agent for which job For questions about your data, pick an agent that can use connectors . A text-only agent can still answer from the conversation, and can work as a Team helper when the lead gives it the data (Team mode). After adding an agent, press Test on its card. It confirms that the model answers before you rely on it."},{"id":"agent-cli","title":"Add a CLI agent","summary":"Use an AI command-line tool that is installed and signed in on this computer.","text":"Use one of the built-in CLIs Open Settings > AI > Agents & models. Find the CLI (Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, Ollama...). If it is not installed, press Install for me and follow the confirmation. Sign in once if the card shows Sign in. Press Test, then switch the agent on. Add your own CLI Press Add agent (CLI) to describe any other command-line AI. Field What to enter Name and description A name for the card, and what the agent is good at. The lead model reads the description when deciding who to delegate to. Command and arguments The program and an argument template that can use {model} , {prompt} , {system_file} , {mcp_config} and {workdir} . Prompt via Whether the prompt is sent on standard input or as an argument. Output Plain text, or JSON lines (then say which field holds the text). MCP Only if the CLI can load an MCP server list from a JSON file; refer to it with {mcp_config} . Environment KEY=value per line, for example API keys. Stored locally and never shown again. Keys for a CLI Keys such as GEMINI_API_KEY go under the agent's edit button > Environment . They stay on this computer. Google retired personal-account sign-in for Gemini CLI on 18 June 2026, so Gemini CLI needs an API key or Vertex AI credentials."},{"id":"agent-api","title":"Add a model by URL and API key","summary":"Connect OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter, Groq, Google AI Studio or a local server.","text":"Add the agent Open Settings > AI > Agents & models and press Add agent (URL + API key). Under Start from pick a well-known provider to fill in the address and format, or leave Custom . Give it a Name and a Description (what it is good at). Type the Base URL , the API key and the model . Press Save, then Test on the new card. The fields Field Notes Base URL For OpenAI-compatible services this is the address ending in /v1 (for example https://api.openai.com/v1 ). For Anthropic it is https://api.anthropic.com . No question mark and no extra path: Raap Nexus adds the endpoint itself. API key Stored on this computer only and never shown again. Local servers such as Ollama need no key. Format OpenAI-compatible (chat/completions) or Anthropic. Tool calling Needs a model that supports function calling. Switch it off for models that do not; the agent then answers from the conversation only. Model Leave empty and Raap Nexus lists what the service offers. Only an agent with tool calling on can use your connectors. A model without it still works as a Team helper."},{"id":"agent-skills","title":"What each agent can use","summary":"Every agent card controls its own connectors, skills and guardrails, so you decide who may use what.","text":"Per-agent control Each agent card in Settings > AI > Agents & models has three boxes: Connectors this agent can use : switches for each connector. For example, keep the ERP for one agent only. The master switch for a connector is on the Connectors page; a connector that is off there is off for every agent. Skills this agent has : removable tags. Press Add skills to tick several at once from a searchable list, including skills that are switched off on the Skills page. Reset to default and Remove all are there too (Skills). Guardrails : rules this agent must follow (Guardrails). Why it matters In Team mode the lead sends each piece of work to the agent whose skills fit, so give each agent only the skills it needs. This also saves tokens, because an agent only carries what you gave it."},{"id":"team-mode","title":"Team mode and the team split","summary":"Let the lead model split a request into parts and hand them to your other agents, in parallel.","text":"What it does With Team on, the model you picked becomes the lead. When a request has several independent parts (data pulls, per-company or per-period work, a second opinion on important numbers) it sends them to your other agents at the same time , checks what comes back and gives you one answer. Turn it on Switch on at least two agents (AI agents). In the chat box press Team. It turns to Team: on . With fewer than two agents it tells you what to add. Ask your question as usual. How a request is split The split is worked out on your computer, with no model call, so the lead does not spend tokens planning: A numbered or bulleted list: one part per item. A fan-out over entities: \"for the companies Alpha, Beta and Gamma\" gives one part per company. Separate actions joined by \"and also\", \"as well as\", a semicolon, or \"and\" before a new action: \"reconcile the debtors and check the stock ageing\" . It does not split when one part depends on another (\"then compare it with that result\"), when a comparison needs both sides (\"compare January and February\"), or when the parts need the same skill. There are at most five parts. Each part gets only the one or two skills it needs, and the least busy agent that can reach your data is chosen. Write a request with several parts as a list, or name the entities, to get the best split. Together with masking If Mask personal details is on, every agent in the team works on masked values, and the team card shows you the real ones."},{"id":"connectors-overview","title":"Connectors: connect your data","summary":"A connector is how the AI looks things up: your ERP, a database or a folder of files. All connectors are read-only.","text":"What a connector is Anything the AI can look things up in is a connector. Raap Nexus never copies your systems; it asks them questions when you ask the AI a question. Connectors you switch off are invisible to the chat. Add a connector Open Settings > Data > Connectors and press Add connector. Choose the type of thing you are connecting (Connector types). Give it a Name (and, if you like, a short description such as \"Sales, stock and customer data for our retail branches\" ). Fill in the address, file or folder, and any login. Use a read-only database user wherever a login is asked. Press Test connection. When it works, press Save. Tick the option to study this system first and an agent explores it read-only for a few minutes, noting what the business is: chart of accounts, customers, salesmen codes, routes, items and which reports work. Every later chat starts with that knowledge (Knowledge). On a connector card Control What it does Switch The master switch. Off means no agent and no chat can use it. Test Checks the connection and lists the tools it offers. Knowledge What the agent knows about this system (Knowledge). Reports For software that answers through report files: which reporting tool it uses and which reports can run (Connector types). Software Which software this is, so Techlogica's profile for it can be linked (Connector types). Edit Change the address, login or description. Always connect with a read-only database user or replica. Raap Nexus only ever runs read statements, but a read-only user is the real protection. Which connector may which agent use? Each agent card has its own switches (What each agent can use), and each dashboard chooses its own connectors (Dashboard settings)."},{"id":"connector-types","title":"Connector types","summary":"MCP servers, SQLite files, folders, SQL databases, OData, REST, GraphQL, Tally and ready-made products.","text":"Local folders, SQLite files and MCP servers work without registering. More types are issued by Techlogica once your computer is registered (Register with Techlogica). Type Use it for You enter Remote MCP server Your ERP's MCP endpoint, or any MCP service The URL (starting with http:// or https://), an optional access token, optional extra headers Local MCP server A tool that runs on this computer A command, for example npx -y some-mcp-server , and its arguments SQLite database A local .db file, read-only SQL The file path Folder of files Excel, Word, PDF, CSV, text, JSON and Markdown files The folder. The AI can list, read and search files inside this folder only SQL Server, MySQL, PostgreSQL Company databases Server, port, database, a read-only user (a connection string such as postgresql://user:password@host:5432/database also works) Oracle Oracle Database 12c or newer, no Oracle client needed Host, port and service name, or a full connect string SAP HANA HANA Cloud (port 443) or on premise Host, port, user. HANA needs SAP's own driver, which Raap Nexus can download after you accept its licence OData An OData service The service root, the address that ends where $metadata starts. Only GET requests are sent REST API Any JSON API A base address, a list of endpoints with sample payloads, and a bearer token, API key or user name. PUT, PATCH and DELETE are never sent GraphQL A GraphQL endpoint The address and saved queries (queries only) Tally TallyPrime on this network The address, usually http://127.0.0.1:9000 Tally in two steps Open TallyPrime with the company loaded. Go to Help (F1) > Settings > Connectivity > Client/Server configuration and set TallyPrime acts as to Server or Both (port 9000). Raap Nexus only sends read (export) requests to Tally. Which software is this? On a connector you can say which software it belongs to. If Techlogica already has a business profile for that software, it is linked and no (token-costing) study is needed. If it has none yet, and you agree to share (What is shared with Techlogica), only the names of tables and columns are sent, never rows, host names or passwords. Report-based software Some software answers through its own report files (FastReport, ActiveReports, JasperStarter and similar). Under the connector's Reports you say which reporting tool it uses. Raap Nexus lists the report files, so the assistant can find the right one, read its rules and run it. The list stays on this computer."},{"id":"connect-product","title":"Connect a product (QuickBooks, Xero and more)","summary":"Ready-made connectors for cloud accounting products. Each product is a Marketplace plan from Techlogica.","text":"What this is For popular cloud accounting products there are ready-made connectors, so you only provide your own details. The list includes QuickBooks Online, Xero, Zoho Books, Sage Accounting and Microsoft Dynamics. Connect one Open Settings > Data > Connectors and press Connect a product. Choose the product, and fill in what it asks (for example your company id and access details). Raap Nexus builds the connector. Then test it and save it like any other connector. If your product is not in the list Each product is a Marketplace plan . It appears here once the plan is active for your company. If you have just added one, or this computer is not registered or cannot reach Techlogica, check Settings > System > Techlogica (Plans and the Marketplace)."},{"id":"knowledge","title":"Knowledge: study a system and search what it learned","summary":"Agents write down what they learn about your systems, keep only high-quality facts and search them when needed, which saves tokens.","text":"Study a system Press Knowledge on a connector card, then Study now . An agent explores the system read-only and writes what it learns: the account heads, customers, salesmen, routes, items and which reports work. It takes a few minutes; you can close the window and come back. The result is a short summary that every later chat using this connector starts with. The rest is searched only when needed. You can correct anything that is wrong and press Save notes ; the facts are rebuilt, keeping only specific, useful ones. Knowledge search Under the connector list, the Knowledge search card decides how facts are found: Search by Meaning Keywords only Built in, nothing to set up. Meaning + keywords, a local model Uses an embedding model installed in Ollama, for example ollama pull nomic-embed-text (about 270 MB). Press Detect afterwards. Meaning + keywords, an API agent Uses that agent's embeddings. This sends the facts to that service. Use Save , Test , Detect and Rebuild on the card. Meaning-based search also improves which skill is chosen for a question (How the assistant chooses skills)."},{"id":"safety","title":"Read-only and approvals (Allow or Deny)","summary":"Tools that only read run at once. Anything that could create, change or delete data pauses and asks you first.","text":"How it works Tools that only read data run straight away. A tool that could create, change or delete data pauses in the chat and asks you to press Allow or Deny first. Automatic workflow runs are read-only. Change the rule Open Settings > System > General > Tool approvals: Ask me first (recommended): the behaviour above. Allow everything: no questions asked. Use it only for connectors you fully trust. Other protections REST, GraphQL and OData connectors never send write requests. Database connectors only run read statements; use a read-only user as well. Every change made in Raap Nexus is recorded in the security log (Data protection and sign-in security)."},{"id":"chat-basics","title":"Ask your data a question","summary":"Type a question in plain words. The agent looks it up in your connectors and answers, often with a table.","text":"Ask Open the chat (New chat). Check the box under the question field: the dashboard it is about, the model that answers, and (if you want) Team . Type your question and press Enter, for example \"Which customers have overdue invoices?\" While the agent works you see what it is doing, step by step, and can press the stop button at any time. Everything it fetches from a connector is shown in the answer so you can check it. Good questions Be specific about the period , company and filter : \"Receivables ageing for March, top 10 overdue customers\" . Words like \"this month\", \"yesterday\" and \"last week\" are worked out when you ask. Say \"pull a new report\" to force fresh data instead of a saved copy (Saved reports). Handling your answers Say \"add this to the dashboard\" and the answer becomes a widget (Pin answers to a dashboard). Copy a table or the whole answer with the buttons under it. Earlier chats are listed in the sidebar by day; search them with Search chats . Clear chats deletes many at once (a chat that is still answering is left alone, and deleted chats cannot be brought back). Voice typing Press the microphone and speak. The browser sends your speech to its own speech service, so it needs an internet connection, and your browser must be allowed to use the microphone for this site. Always check important figures. Answers come from your connectors through the agent you picked, and an AI can still misread a question."},{"id":"chat-skills","title":"Use a skill in chat","summary":"Type / to pick a skill for one message, or let the assistant load the skills a question needs.","text":"What a skill is A skill is an instruction pack: how to reconcile a ledger, how to audit a spreadsheet, how a tax return is prepared. The assistant loads a skill only when a question needs one, so skills cost nothing until used (Skills). Pick one yourself Type / in the question field. A list of skills opens; keep typing to filter it and press Enter to choose one. That skill is used for this one message. Let the assistant choose You do not have to pick. Before the model is called, Raap Nexus reads your question and gives the agent only the few skills that fit, which saves tokens. It gets better with use (How the assistant chooses skills)."},{"id":"chat-dashboard","title":"Pin answers to a dashboard and schedule them","summary":"Turn an answer into a widget, refresh it later, or have the same question asked on a schedule and sent to you.","text":"Add to the dashboard After an answer you like, say \"add this to the dashboard\" . The agent creates the widget on the dashboard this chat is about. You can also ask for a whole view at once, for example \"Build a KPI overview and add it to my dashboard\" or \"Make a monthly Budget tab based on the last three years' trial balance\" . Ask again on a schedule Any question can be repeated on a schedule, with fresh data each time, and the answer sent to you. Choose the schedule, and pick where it goes: an in-app alert, an email, or both. Email needs the email server set up first under Automations > Email settings. Words like \"this month\" are worked out again each time it runs (Automations). Refresh later Widgets built from reports remember how to refresh. See Dashboards for how a refresh works."},{"id":"dashboards","title":"Dashboards, tabs and widgets","summary":"An animated dashboard with tabs, per-widget period buttons, maps and 15+ chart types, built by asking the AI.","text":"The dashboard Open a dashboard from the sidebar. At the top you see its name, a summary strip of headline findings, and the actions. Below, the tabs group related widgets, and a + adds a tab. Button What it does Dashboards Switch to another dashboard. Ask in chat Open a chat about this dashboard. Comments Read and write comments on the dashboard and on widgets. Refresh data Pull the reports behind the charts again (details). Share Give people access (Share a dashboard). Present Full-screen presentation mode. Widgets Widgets show a number, a chart, a table or a map. Each can have its own period buttons (for example Quarter) so one widget can show a different range from its neighbour. There are more than 15 chart types, including gauges, trend lines, rankings and maps. Build by asking You rarely build a widget by hand. Ask in chat and say \"add it to the dashboard\" . Drag widgets to reorder them; hover for the menu to rename or remove one. What-if and dashboard tools A period selector re-states the widgets for a month, quarter, year or custom range. A what-if panel lets you change an assumption and see the effect on the figures. Maps colour regions by a value, with the places taken from the data."},{"id":"dashboards-share","title":"Share a dashboard, comments and refresh","summary":"Four roles decide what each person can do. Refresh re-pulls the reports behind your charts.","text":"Share On a dashboard press Share (for the dashboard's admins). Pick a person and a role: Role Can Viewer See the dashboard and its widgets. Commentator Also comment on the dashboard and widgets, and chat about it. Editor Also add, change, move and delete widgets and tabs (also through chat). Admin Also rename or delete the dashboard and manage who it is shared with. The owner and a dashboard's creator are always admin. People without access do not see the dashboard at all. To chat, a person needs the chat permission and at least Commentator on a dashboard (Users and permissions). Share a link The Share window can also give you a link for a shared dashboard. The link uses your domain if you set one, otherwise the running phone-mode address, otherwise your network address (Domain, port and phone mode). Refresh data Refresh data makes an agent pull the same reports again: only entries that are posted or confirmed, continuing from the date each chart last covered, and rebuilding a chart from the start only when its opening or closing balance changed. Widgets built before this feature existed may ask you to rebuild them once. Comments Commentators and above can write comments; a Viewer can read them. Comments are listed on the dashboard and on each widget."},{"id":"dashboards-settings","title":"Dashboard settings and saved reports","summary":"Choose which connectors each dashboard may use, and how saved reports are reused.","text":"Dashboards page Open Settings > Data > Dashboards. Each dashboard has its own tabs and its own connectors. In chat you pick which dashboard you are working on, and the AI can only use that dashboard's connectors and adds widgets only to it. Press New dashboard (or use an existing one) and give it a name. Choose which connectors it may use. Dashboards made by people without settings access start with no connectors until an administrator adds them. Keep at least one dashboard: the last one cannot be deleted. Deleting a dashboard moves its chats to your first one. Saved reports Reports you pull are kept encrypted on this computer, so the same report is not pulled again and again. Under Settings > System > General > Saved reports: When a saved copy exists : ask once per question (recommended), reuse it, or always pull a new one. Reuse without asking if it is newer than : always ask, 10 minutes, 30 minutes or 1 hour. Keep saved reports for : 1, 7 or 30 days. Reports for the current month, current year or today are always pulled fresh. Custom instructions Under the same General page, Custom instructions are added to every new conversation. Good for business context, currency and fiscal calendar, for example: Always answer in English. Our financial year starts in April. Amounts are in AED. Prefer tables."},{"id":"automations","title":"Workflows and templates","summary":"A workflow runs on a schedule or a trigger and does its steps one after another: pull data, check it, then email or alert you.","text":"What a workflow is A workflow is a list of steps that runs by itself: ask an agent to pull data, check it, then email or alert you. Automatic runs are read-only , and every run is logged. Schedules run only while Raap Nexus is running, so keep it on, or choose start when I sign in in the installer. Start from a template Open Automations > Templates (or press From a template on the Workflows tab). Pick one. Ready-made ones include a daily audit of unposted journals, a reviewed audit with a sign-off, a month-end close pack, a weekly overdue receivables digest, a monthly budget-vs-actual variance, a daily sales flash, a multi-level approval and an agent that answers when a web link is called. Answer the few questions it asks: the company, the time, who to email, which dashboard's connectors and which agent. Press Run now to test it. Nothing runs until you do, or switch it on. The Morning briefing at the top of the Workflows tab is a ready-made one: each morning, yesterday's sales, anything unusual and the approvals waiting, sent as an alert, an email, or both. Build your own Press New workflow, name it, choose when it starts and add steps. Starts Meaning Manual You press Run. Every day, week or month At the time you set. Every few minutes or hours A repeating interval. A web link Another system calls a link Raap Nexus creates when you save (GET or POST). The data it sends is available as {{ trigger.body.name }} . A customer message A WhatsApp or Instagram message arrived (Customer channels). Step What it does Ask an agent Gives an agent a task; it uses your connectors, skills and the dashboard you pick. Refresh a dashboard Re-runs the reports behind a dashboard's charts and updates them. Call a connector tool Calls one read-only tool directly, with no AI. Check a condition Stops here (as skipped) unless the condition is true. Ask for approval Several approval levels with signatures (Approvals). Send an email, Raise an alert Tell someone the result. An alert can be sent on WhatsApp in one click. Message a customer Sends a WhatsApp or Instagram message. Customer guardrails are checked first. Call a web address Calls another system with GET or POST. Use a web page Opens a page and reads it, or clicks and types. Needs the browser tool (Advanced setup). Make a file An Excel, Word or PDF from a dashboard's data. No AI is used, so no tokens are spent and the figures are exactly the dashboard's. Set variables Computes values for later steps. In any text field you can use values such as {{ today }} , {{ month_name }} , {{ vars.company }} and earlier results like {{ steps.audit.answer }} . Type {{ for suggestions. Check what happened Each workflow lists its runs with a status (OK, failed, waiting for you, skipped) and what every step did. You can re-run a run, stop one that is running, and keep answers you chose to remember so the agent does not ask again."},{"id":"approvals","title":"Approvals","summary":"Multi-level approvals with signatures. The workflow pauses until everyone has decided, and a signed record is kept.","text":"How it works An approval step asks people to approve a request: an amount, a customer, any record. Levels run in order, and a level whose rule is false is skipped. The workflow waits until everyone who must decide has decided. Start from the Multi-level approval template under Automations > Templates, or add an Ask for approval step to a workflow. Name each level and list its approvers, one per line: a name, an email and/or WhatsApp number, @username for one Raap Nexus user, or level:2 for everyone at approval level 2 (give people a level under Settings > People). Write a rule for when a level applies, for example number(trigger.body.amount) >= 10000 . Leave it empty to always ask. Choose who is emailed the signed record. What approvers see Each approver gets a private link by email (or you can send it on WhatsApp from the Approvals tab). They review the request, then approve or decline. By approving they confirm the request: their name, signature, the time and their network address are recorded together with a fingerprint of the request. A person with an earlier level still to decide cannot decide yet; they are told to open the link again later. Once a request is closed, nothing more is needed. The Approvals tab Automations > Approvals lists requests waiting for approvers and the signed record of the finished ones. You can remind an approver or cancel a request (approvers can then no longer decide it). If approvers are outside this computer or network, set a public address or use phone mode so their links open (Domain, port and phone mode)."},{"id":"workflow-engines","title":"Variables, email, alerts and advanced setup","summary":"Nexus variables, the email server, alerts, the browser tool and the optional n8n, Node-RED and Elsa engines.","text":"Variables Everything in your Raap Nexus has a name you can use inside workflows, so nothing is typed twice: users, dashboards (with their connectors and companies), agents, skills and connectors. Open Automations > Variables, click a field to copy its name and paste it into a step. It is replaced with the real value each time the workflow runs. Email settings Automations > Email settings holds the mail server used by Send an email steps. It is stored on this computer only. For Gmail use smtp.gmail.com , STARTTLS and an app password; for Microsoft 365 use smtp.office365.com , STARTTLS. There is a test button. Alerts Alerts lists results and failures raised by your workflows. Send on WhatsApp opens WhatsApp with the message ready (there is no WhatsApp API in this; you press send). To get alerts as notifications, see My account and notifications. Advanced setup The built-in workflows cover schedules, agents, email, alerts and approvals. If you want more, Raap Nexus can add a visual engine next to it, run it privately on this computer (reachable only through Raap Nexus and your sign-in) and connect it to your agents. Nothing is installed system-wide. Engine Good for Download n8n A visual editor with 400+ ready connections (Google Sheets, Slack, Telegram, Outlook, databases, webhooks). A private Node.js (about 38 MB) if needed, then n8n (about 1 GB, usually 5 to 15 minutes). Node-RED Flow-based automation with thousands of community nodes (MQTT and IoT, Modbus, databases, Telegram, email, HTTP). Popular on factory floors. Node.js if needed, then Node-RED (about 150 MB). Elsa Workflows An open-source .NET engine with a visual designer, long-running workflows, timers and JavaScript expressions. The .NET SDK (about 250 MB) if needed, then a build of about 1 GB. You accept the licence first. Browser tool Work on websites that have no connection to plug into: a supplier portal, a daily download, a form. agent-browser (about 55 MB), checked against its published checksum. Each engine page has the same buttons: install, start, stop, open, and remove completely. Raap Nexus workflow templates can be added to the engine as ready-to-edit flows, each using your agents, email, alerts and approvals. A flow can ask an agent with a small call to Raap Nexus, and agents answer read-only from your connectors. The browser tool, safely Every Use a web page step lists the sites it may visit; a page outside the list is left at once. Reading is free. A step that clicks or types needs an approved approval step before it, or your explicit tick on that step. For a site that needs a login, open a window, sign in yourself and press Done. Raap Nexus never sees your password. The kept login is stored encrypted. Websites have their own terms. Many do not allow automated use and may block the account. For WhatsApp use the official channel under Settings > Channels."},{"id":"skills","title":"Skills","summary":"Instruction packs the assistant loads only when a question needs one, so they cost nothing until used.","text":"What skills are Skills are instruction packs. The assistant sees a short list and asks for the skill it wants, so a skill costs nothing until it is used. Skills for a specific software, such as ERPNext or Tally, come from Techlogica and only when this company uses that software. Built-in skills Area Skills Finance Ledger reconciliation, financial statements (P&L), financial statements and tax, accounting adjustments, close commentary, financial intelligence Tax Tax consultant and accountant (UAE, Saudi Arabia, Bahrain, Qatar, Kuwait, Oman, India, UK, US), tax jurisdictions, tax compliance and filing, tax communication, tax risk monitoring, regulatory monitoring Data and files Business analysis, spreadsheet audit, connector study Dashboards and automation Dashboard design, dashboard refresh, workflow builder Turn skills on or off, and write your own Open Settings > AI > Skills. Switch a skill on to let the assistant load it when a question needs it. Most are not loaded by default. Press Add skill to write your own: a name, a description and the instructions. A skill you write stays on your computer. Use Reset on a built-in skill to restore its original text. The page can also import the finance and small-business skills of Claude plugins installed on this computer; they arrive switched off. Where skills are used In chat: type / to choose one (Skills in chat). Per agent: the Skills tags on each agent card (What each agent can use). Automatically: the router offers only the skills that fit the question (How the assistant chooses skills)."},{"id":"guardrails","title":"Guardrails","summary":"Rules an agent must follow however it is asked, with optional checks on what it writes.","text":"What a guardrail is A guardrail is a rule in plain words that is given to the agent as a hard rule above every request, skill and tool result. It can also carry patterns : whatever the agent writes is checked against them before anyone sees it, in workflow results, saved chats and customer replies. Built-in guardrails Guardrail What it does No financial information Customers never get company financial data. Prices written in the company knowledge may be quoted, nothing else. No personal data of customers or staff Never reveal who else bought, wrote or works here, and never ask for card or ID numbers. Stay on topic Only talk about the company, its products and how to reach the team. No promises or professional advice No guarantees, no legal, medical or financial advice. Mask personal details Replaces real names and numbers with stand-ins before they reach the model (read more). Older SQL Server Tells the agent how to query SQL Server 2008 and 2008 R2. Where a guardrail applies All agents : every agent follows it, unless you take it off one agent in Settings > Agents. Chosen agents : add it with the Guardrails tag box on an agent card. Customer channels : every WhatsApp and Instagram reply follows it, whichever agent writes the reply. Write your own Press Add guardrail. Write the rule in plain words, for example Never mention competitors by name. If asked about them, say you can only talk about our own products. Optionally add patterns: a word or a regular expression, not case sensitive, for example (revenue|profit|salary) . A match blocks the whole reply (the fallback text is sent instead) or redacts just that part. There is a special check that blocks a reply naming an amount of money that is not written in the company knowledge. Choose where it applies, then save. Use the test box to try it before relying on it."},{"id":"mask-pii","title":"Mask personal details","summary":"The AI sees stable stand-ins such as Customer_0001 instead of real names, e-mails, phones and bank or tax numbers. Your tools and your screen still use the real values.","text":"What it does The model reasons on relationships (this customer owes that much, these two invoices share a supplier), not on real names. So every identifying value is replaced, for the whole conversation, by a stable stand-in: Customer_0001 , Supplier_0002 , user0003@masked.example , Phone_0004 . The same value always gets the same stand-in, so grouping, matching, duplicates and joins give the same answer as with the real data. Your tools still run on the real values : a query for Customer_0001 runs against the real customer. You read the real values in the answer, even when a stand-in arrives in pieces while the answer streams. The map of stand-ins stays on this computer, sealed with its key, so numbering survives a restart. Turn it on Open Settings > AI > Guardrails. On Mask personal details , switch on All agents, or add the guardrail to chosen agents on their cards. Optionally adjust the lists below (the options are listed below) and press Save . Running chats pick the change up on their next message. Options Option Use it for Names to always mask One per line, for example the names of your biggest customers. Hidden even in your first question. Extra columns that hold personal details Your own column names, with the kind of value they hold: Customer: acct_holder , Phone: whatsapp_no . Columns to leave as they are A column that looks personal but the model needs. Try it Paste a few rows of data to see exactly what the model would receive. What is masked, and what is not Masked: columns called customer, supplier, vendor, employee, email, phone, address, IBAN, tax id and similar (in JSON, tables, CSV and \"Key: value\" lines), then patterns anywhere: e-mail addresses, phone numbers with a country code, IBANs, card numbers, Emirates ID and SSN. Not masked, on purpose: amounts, dates, quantities, account codes, item names, barcodes, cities and countries, because the model needs them to calculate and compare. This lowers exposure. It is not anonymisation: amounts and dates can still identify a company to someone determined. A name typed in your very first message is only masked if it is in your list or has already appeared in data. It is never applied to replies to customers. With Team mode Every agent in a team works on masked values, and you see the real ones on the team card (Team mode)."},{"id":"skill-routing","title":"How the assistant chooses skills","summary":"Only the skills a question needs go to the model, which saves tokens. It improves with use, and sharing what it learned is optional.","text":"Why it matters Every skill put into a prompt costs tokens on every question. So before the model is called, Raap Nexus scores each available skill against your question and gives the model only the few that fit: the best one in full when it is clearly right, a short list of the next best, and a search tool for the rest. How it scores Part What it does Words Matches the words of your question against each skill's name, description and text, weighting rare words more. Meaning Compares meaning with embeddings, so \"invoices that do not match what the customer owes\" finds a reconciliation skill. Needs an embedding source set up under Settings > Data > Knowledge search; otherwise it is skipped. Learned When the model had to ask for a skill it was not offered, or put one aside, the words of that question are tied to (or away from) that skill. This is what makes it better over time. What is kept on this computer is only word stems of questions, counted per skill: never the question itself. Sharing (optional, off by default) Under Settings > System > Techlogica the card How the assistant chooses skills has the switch Share skill-choosing training . Off : everything stays here. On : only a skill's name, one word stem and three counts leave this computer (shown, asked for, set aside), and you receive what other installations learned. Press Exactly what would be sent to see the full list first. Never sent: your questions, documents, figures, names, or skills you wrote yourself. A received hint is used lightly, and only after enough separate installations and companies agree. An administrator at Techlogica can reject any of it."},{"id":"agent-history","title":"Agent history and cost","summary":"Every job an agent did: your chats, tasks handed to a team member and automation runs.","text":"Where to look Settings > AI > Agent history lists every job an agent did: your chats, tasks the lead handed to a team member (and which skill sent it there) and automation runs. Click an agent to filter. Tokens The page also shows token use per agent. Where an agent does not report its usage, the figure is estimated (around 4 characters per token) and marked as such. It helps you see which agents and skills cost the most and tune them (What each agent can use). No work recorded yet? It appears here as agents answer chats, handle team tasks and run automations."},{"id":"channels","title":"Customer channels: WhatsApp and Instagram","summary":"Let agents answer customers using only the company knowledge you write. No ERP data ever reaches a customer reply.","text":"What it does Raap Nexus can answer customers on WhatsApp and Instagram itself, with no extra app. Each WhatsApp number or Instagram account is a line , so Support and General enquiries can have different agents, reply styles, knowledge and limits. A customer who asks for a person, or writes too often, is handed to your team with an alert and the bot goes quiet for them. Replies are written without any connector and without tools . The agent only knows the company knowledge you write below, so nothing from your ERP or reports can reach a customer. Guardrails marked for customer channels are checked on every reply. Connect WhatsApp Create a Meta app at developers.facebook.com (type Business ) and add the WhatsApp product. In WhatsApp > API setup copy the Phone number ID and the WhatsApp Business Account ID . In Business settings > System users, create a user, give it your app and WhatsApp account, and generate a permanent token with whatsapp_business_messaging and whatsapp_business_management . In Raap Nexus enter the Meta app ID and app secret, add a line with those details, and press Turn on . It checks the token, subscribes to messages and registers its address with Meta for you. Connect Instagram Use an Instagram Business or Creator account. In your Meta app add the Instagram product (Instagram API with Instagram login). In Instagram > API setup add the account and generate an access token with the messaging permission. Copy the Instagram app ID and app secret. Add a line in Raap Nexus and press Turn on . Until Meta approves your app for messaging (app review), only accounts that have a role on the app can message the bot. Meta needs a secure public address to reach Raap Nexus. Bind a domain under Settings > Domain & port, or turn on phone mode (Domain, port and phone mode). Company knowledge The assistant answers customers only from the entries you write, and says a colleague will follow up when something is not there. Add entries as company profile, products and services (name, what it is, price if you want it quoted) and questions with answers. You can also read text from a PDF, or read products from one of your connectors (read-only): you choose what to keep, and only that text becomes knowledge. Write only what you are happy for any customer to read: no financial figures, no personal data, nothing internal. Pieces with financial words are left out unless you tick them. Line settings The agent that answers and an optional reply style (product information, about the company, sales assistant, support and FAQ). Reply automatically : turn it off to only collect messages and alert your team. Conversations : see every conversation, resolve it, send a message yourself, or hand a customer back to the bot. Turning a line off stops it answering; its past conversations stay for 90 days. WhatsApp and Instagram are products of Meta Platforms. Raap Nexus is not affiliated with or endorsed by Meta."},{"id":"users","title":"Users and permissions","summary":"Add people, choose what each may do, and share dashboards with them. Everyone signs in with their own username and password.","text":"The owner and everyone else The person who first signs up is the owner : every permission, always, and that cannot be changed. The owner (or anyone given Manage users ) adds people under Settings > People. Add a person Press Add user. Enter their name, username, email and phone, and a password (at least 8 characters, not a common one). Choose a permission set (below), or Custom to tick each permission. Pick the dashboards this person may see, and optionally an approval level so they can sign approvals (Approvals). Permission sets Set For Administrator Everything except managing users. Analyst Chat, their own dashboards, and seeing automations. Approver Signs approvals and opens dashboards shared with them. No chat. Viewer Only opens dashboards shared with them. Custom Choose each permission yourself. The individual permissions Permission Allows Use chat and agents Ask questions about dashboards they have access to (commentator or higher). Create their own dashboards Make new dashboards and share them (they are admin of those). See automations View workflows, run history and alerts. Manage automations Create, edit and run workflows; email settings; see every approval. Manage agents, connectors and settings Agents, skills, connectors, phone mode and general settings. This includes connecting programs on this computer, so give it only to people you trust. Manage users Create users and change their permissions. Give this only to people you trust fully. Looking after people Lost phone and recovery codes: open the person's edit window and switch their second step off. They are signed out and can sign in again with the password, or must set it up again if the owner requires it. Removing someone: they lose access, their chats are deleted and their dashboards go back to the owner. To chat, a person needs the chat permission and at least Commentator on a dashboard; the dashboard decides which connectors the chat can use."},{"id":"security","title":"Data protection and sign-in security","summary":"Encryption tied to this computer, the recovery code, a second sign-in step with an authenticator app, and a tamper-evident security log.","text":"Data protection Your database, business metadata, workspace and tool data are encrypted on this computer and tied to its hardware identity. A copy of the data folder on another computer is unreadable. Open Settings > System > Data protection. Recovery code Without it, a hardware change or a move to a new computer means the data cannot be recovered. Press Show my recovery code, write it down or print it and keep it somewhere safe, away from this computer. It is shown only once. If you lose it, press Create a new recovery code: the old one stops working immediately. Anyone with the recovery code and a copy of your data folder can open the data. Treat it like a master key. Second step when signing in An authenticator app (Google Authenticator, Microsoft Authenticator, Authy, 1Password and others) adds a 6-digit code to the password. Open Settings > Account > My account and find Second step when signing in . Scan the picture with your authenticator app and type the code it shows. Save the ten recovery codes shown. Each works once if you lose the phone, and they are shown only now. The owner can require the second step for people. Someone it applies to who has not set it up can sign in but do nothing else until they do. If you lose your phone and recovery codes, another administrator switches your second step off under Users; if you are the only one, run python raapnexus.py mfa-reset USERNAME on this computer and restart Raap Nexus. Security log Every sign-in (and failed one), sign-out and every change made in Raap Nexus is recorded with who did it and from where. What people typed, passwords and agent answers are never written to it. Nobody can edit or delete an event, and Check the log is intact shows if the file was tampered with. You can search it, export it as CSV, and get an access review (who can do what)."},{"id":"access","title":"Domain, port and phone mode","summary":"Give Raap Nexus its own web address, choose where it listens, or open it on your phone from anywhere with a secure tunnel.","text":"Domain and port Open Settings > System > Domain & port. Domain name Give Raap Nexus a proper address, for example https://nexus.yourcompany.com or http://192.168.1.20:8787 . Once it is set, phone access, shared-dashboard links, approval links and the WhatsApp messages all use this address, and the phone-mode tunnel is not used. The full address people will type goes in Address ; press Save address . A company web address of the form your-name.raapnexus.com is also available as an add-on, per site, ordered under Settings > System > Techlogica > Marketplace. Listen on Choice Meaning Only this computer The safe choice. Use it behind a reverse proxy or tunnel on this computer. All network interfaces Others on your network can reach it. Allow the port in the firewall; to reach it from the internet, forward it on your router. This is plain HTTP, so prefer a proxy or tunnel outside your office. Changes to port and listening address need a restart. Adding the lock (HTTPS) Raap Nexus speaks plain HTTP. For a domain with a lock, put one of these in front of it and point your domain's DNS at the machine (or the tunnel): Cloudflare Tunnel (recommended): create a named tunnel in the Cloudflare dashboard and route your hostname to the local address. No router changes, and Cloudflare provides HTTPS. Keep Listen on: only this computer . A reverse proxy such as nginx. Behind a proxy, Raap Nexus recognises your domain, uses secure cookies when the proxy says the connection is HTTPS and sees visitors' real addresses from the X-Forwarded-For header. The page shows a ready-made configuration. Phone mode Phone mode opens Raap Nexus on your phone from anywhere. It starts a secure https tunnel (Cloudflare) to this computer and opens WhatsApp with the link ready so you can send it to yourself. This computer must stay on, and the tunnel switches itself off after a while. Click the phone button at the bottom of the sidebar. If asked, let Raap Nexus download the Cloudflare tunnel program (about 55 MB, kept in the data folder, no account needed). Optionally type your WhatsApp number (with country code, digits only) so your own chat opens directly. Press Turn on phone mode , send the message to yourself, and open the link on your phone. Turn off ends it. While phone mode is on, anyone who has the link can reach the sign-in page. Use a strong password, do not forward the link, and turn phone mode off when you are done. The address changes each time it is turned on, so an app installed on an iPhone from it stops working then. For a permanent address, set your own domain. If your phone cannot open the link on mobile data, that network may block the trycloudflare.com domain: try another network or set your own domain."},{"id":"general","title":"General settings","summary":"Appearance, saved reports, tool approvals, custom instructions and a full export of your chats and dashboards.","text":"Settings > System > General holds the settings that apply to the whole workspace. Card What it controls Read more Appearance Language, theme (system, light, dark) and accent colour. Languages and appearance Saved reports Whether a report pulled recently is reused, and how long copies are kept. Dashboard settings Tool approvals Ask first before a tool changes data, or allow everything. Read-only and approvals Custom instructions Text added to every new conversation: business context, currency, fiscal calendar, tone. Dashboard settings Your data Everything lives in the data folder, encrypted. Export chats & dashboard downloads a JSON copy any time. Data protection Credits and licenses Third-party software used by Raap Nexus and its licences."},{"id":"health","title":"Health, support and housekeeping","summary":"A check of this computer and its setup, a diagnostics file you can send to support, and daily housekeeping.","text":"Check this computer Open Settings > System > Health & support and press Check this computer for the full list. Also check the network tests the connections that need the internet. Local folders, SQLite files and MCP servers work without any connection to Techlogica. Getting set up lists what is done, still to do and optional: your first connector, your recovery code, registering with Techlogica. Needs attention says what is wrong and what to do about it, with a Go button. Support information If Techlogica asks for diagnostics, this builds a file with versions, the health results and the state of your set-up. It contains no business data, no connector settings, passwords, keys or email addresses . It is shown in full first and nothing is sent: you save it and send it yourself. Two options: include connector names (otherwise they appear as connector-1, connector-2) and include the last lines of the application log (secrets and personal details are removed, but a log is free text, so please read it). Housekeeping The database is compacted and tidied by itself once a day, in the quiet hours and only while nobody is working. Nothing you wrote is removed: chats, dashboards, comments, automations and the agent history are left alone."},{"id":"versions","title":"Updates and version history","summary":"See what is new in every version, and update with one click on a computer registered with Techlogica.","text":"Version history Settings > System > Version history lists every version with what was new, improved, fixed or secured, and what is coming (a plan, not a promise). It works for everyone, with or without registration. A dot beside the page name tells you a newer version is ready. Update Register this computer with Techlogica (Register with Techlogica). New versions arrive for registered computers, which check every half hour. When one is available it is downloaded in the background and checked. Read what changed. If an update changes things your saved questions rely on, you are told to review it first. Press the install button from the computer where Raap Nexus runs : a phone or a shared link cannot replace the program. Raap Nexus closes, installs the update and opens again, usually in about a minute. Your data, settings and connectors stay as they are. Anything running at that moment (a chat answer, a workflow) is stopped, so pick a quiet moment. If it does not come back by itself, start it from the Start menu (Windows) or the Applications folder (Mac). Your data is untouched, and if an install fails you stay on the version you had."},{"id":"account","title":"My account and notifications","summary":"Change your own password and details, set the second sign-in step, and choose how alerts reach you.","text":"My account Open Settings > Account > My account. Change your name, username, email, phone and password (at least 8 characters, not a common password; leave the password blank to keep the current one). The owner sees a note that they can add other users; everyone else sees which permission set they have. This page also has the Second step when signing in (Data protection and sign-in security). Notifications Settings > Account > Notifications: alerts raised by your workflows (results, failures, approvals waiting) can pop up as notifications, even when Raap Nexus is closed (the computer running it must be on). This is personal: each person sets up their own devices. Alerts on this browser : press Enable and allow notifications. Browsers only allow push notifications on https addresses or on this computer (localhost), so through your domain or a phone-mode link use https. If you blocked them, allow them in the browser's site settings (the lock icon) and press Enable again. Alerts on your phone : on Android, open Raap Nexus in the phone app and switch alerts on there. On an iPhone, open Raap Nexus over https, add it to the Home Screen, open it from there and enable browser notifications. You see alerts addressed to you, and general alerts if you may see automations."},{"id":"mobile","title":"Use Raap Nexus on your phone","summary":"Open it in a phone browser, install it as an app, or use the Android app. The data stays on your computer.","text":"How it works Raap Nexus always runs on your computer. Your phone is a window onto it, so the computer must be on and reachable. There are three ways to reach it: Way Good for Phone mode Quick access from anywhere with a secure tunnel, no router settings (Domain, port and phone mode). Your own domain A permanent address that works for the Android app, shared dashboards and approval links. Wi-Fi Start Raap Nexus (phone access) from the Start menu for the same network. Install it as an app A small card at the bottom of the screen offers to install Raap Nexus as an app (Chrome and Edge from their own button). On an iPhone, open it in Safari, choose Share , then Add to Home Screen , and open it from there. Choose Don't ask again to hide the card. The Android app Install the .apk from Techlogica. Give it the address of your computer: your domain, or the phone-mode link. Sign in with your normal username and password. For alerts, switch them on in Settings > Account > Notifications inside the app: it shows each alert as a notification, with no Google account or push service involved. Allow Raap Nexus to run in the background if alerts arrive late. On a phone, Raap Nexus opens on your dashboard first, and the layout adapts to the narrow screen."},{"id":"register","title":"Register with Techlogica","summary":"Tell Techlogica who you are and which software you use, paste the key you receive, and unlock your plan, connectors and updates.","text":"Why register You can use Raap Nexus without registering. Your local folders, SQLite files and MCP servers work as they are. Registering with Techlogica gives you: The connectors issued to your company (for example SQL databases, OData, REST, GraphQL, Tally and ready-made products). A plan with more users, dashboards, channels and features. Updates, which arrive for registered computers (Updates and version history). Business profiles for your software, so you do not spend tokens teaching the assistant. Register Open Settings > System > Techlogica. Under Register with Techlogica enter your Company name and the E-mail where Techlogica should send your key. Choose your Software , and How Raap Nexus connects to it (or Not sure). A database such as SQL Server or Oracle is a connector, not your software: choose your software and the connector separately. Press Register. Techlogica emails you a personal key. Paste the key (press I already have a key if you have it already) and activate. The connectors issued to your company now work on this computer. Other ways to activate If Techlogica gave you an address and a public key instead, enter those: the public key cannot do anything by itself. Unregister You can unregister this computer at any time. The connectors issued by Techlogica stop working here until you enter a key again; your own connectors and data are not affected. Registering is also what lets this computer receive updates. After you register, press Check now to see your plan straight away."},{"id":"plan","title":"Your plan and the Marketplace","summary":"See your limits, ask for more users, dashboards, channels and products, and pay for add-ons.","text":"Your plan The Your plan card on the Techlogica page lists what you have against what your plan allows: users, dashboards, channels, features. The free plan is the starting point; nothing you already have is ever removed when limits change. Marketplace Ask for more: extra users, dashboards, channels, ready-made product connectors (QuickBooks Online, Xero, Sage, Microsoft Dynamics and others) and add-ons such as a company web address. Techlogica approves each request. After approval press Check now (or wait for the automatic check) and it is yours. Your plan is checked with Techlogica online whenever you add something. Items that cost money show a payment step; you can see your payment history on the same page. Connectors from Techlogica The page also lists the connectors issued to your company and the software information Techlogica holds for it, with a link to see what the assistant already knows (Knowledge)."},{"id":"sharing","title":"What is shared with Techlogica","summary":"Nothing about your business data is shared. Two optional, off-by-default switches share how your software works and how skills are chosen.","text":"The two switches Both are on the Techlogica page, both are off by default , and you can turn either off at any time (what was already shared stays with Techlogica). Switch What is shared What is never shared What the assistant learns about your software Notes on how the software works: what a table means, which report answers what. If Techlogica has no profile yet, the names of its tables and columns. Customers, amounts, numbers, rows, host names, passwords. They are refused and stay on this computer. Share skill-choosing training A skill's name, one word stem and three counts. In return you receive what other installations learned. Your questions, documents, figures, names, and skills you wrote. Both show you exactly what would be sent before you switch them on, and you can delete individual learnings. See How the assistant chooses skills for the second. Besides these Registering sends your company name, email and software so a key can be issued. Plan checks and update checks contact Techlogica. The diagnostics file (Health and support) is shown to you and only sent if you send it. Your AI model provider (for a URL agent) receives what you ask and the data the agent fetches to answer it; use Mask personal details to limit what identifies people in that."},{"id":"sites","title":"Sites and group finance","summary":"See several companies or locations on one page, with their figures added up in one currency.","text":"What it is If your business has several sites, each with its own Raap Nexus, a group hub shows them together. Seeing a company's locations on one page is arranged by Techlogica: ask them to make a hub and add your sites to its group. The Sites page appears in the sidebar only on the company's group hub (Techlogica decides which computer that is), and only for people who manage settings. On each site Register the site with Techlogica (Register with Techlogica). Under Settings > System > Techlogica find Shared with the group hub and choose which dashboards the hub may look at (view only), or all of them. Set the site's base currency and choose which figures to share. The hub receives monthly totals only (never entries or names), and only for the figures you choose. On the hub Open a site to see its own shared dashboards. The group page adds the sites up in one currency, with a table By site . Add exchange rates: type the currency and the value of one unit (if 1 AED is 0.27 USD, type AED and 0.27). Leave the month empty for a rate that applies to every month, or add a month such as 2026-03 when that month's rate differs. The average rate is used for revenue, expenses and profit; the closing rate for cash, receivables and similar balances. Trading between your sites is not removed. Drag a figure, or use its menu, to move it."},{"id":"troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting","summary":"Common messages and what to do about them.","text":"What you see What to do The agent answers \"Failed to authenticate\" or \"The CLI exited with code 1\" The AI command-line tool is signed out. Run it once in a terminal and sign in again (for example claude , or codex login ), or press Sign in on the agent card, then press Test . \"... cannot use connectors, so it only answers from the conversation\" That agent is text-only or has tool calling switched off. Pick an agent that can use connectors, or switch tool calling on in its settings if the model supports it (URL agents). \"Could not connect\" when saving a connector Check the address, the login and that the system is running and reachable from this computer. Use Test connection and read the message. Use a read-only user. For Tally, the company must be open and the server setting on (Connector types). The Team chip says it needs two agents Switch on a second agent (Team mode). My request was not split into parts It is one piece of work, or the parts depend on each other. Write it as a list. A connector does not appear in the chat It is switched off on the Connectors page, off for that agent, or not chosen for the dashboard this chat is about (What each agent can use, Dashboard settings). \"To chat they need the chat permission and at least Commentator on a dashboard\" Give the person the permission under People and share a dashboard with them (Users and permissions). The model saw a name that should have been masked Add it under Names to always mask or its column under Extra columns , and try it in the Try it box (Mask personal details). A report is out of date Say \"pull a new report\", or change the saved-report settings (Dashboard settings). Approval links do not open for someone outside Set a domain or turn on phone mode so links point somewhere they can reach (Domain, port and phone mode). WhatsApp or Instagram says the address is not secure Meta needs a secure public address. Set a domain or turn on phone mode (Customer channels). A schedule did not run Schedules only run while Raap Nexus is running. Keep it on, or choose start when I sign in in the installer. Port already in use, or it opens an old copy Raap Nexus is probably already running; launching it again just opens the running copy. Stop it first with python raapnexus.py stop , or choose another port with --port . I lost my recovery code Create a new one under Settings > System > Data protection. The old one stops working at once (Data protection). Still stuck? Open Settings > System > Health & support, press Check this computer and follow what it says. If Techlogica asks for diagnostics, build the support information there (Health and support). Contact Techlogica at info@techlogica.com or www.techlogica.com."},{"id":"faq","title":"Frequently asked questions","summary":"Short answers about data, cost, models and limits.","text":"Does my data leave my computer? The app, database and settings stay on your computer. What the agent fetches from a connector to answer a question goes to the AI model you chose, because that is how it can answer. Local models (Ollama) keep even that on your computer, and Mask personal details replaces identifying values before they go to a model. Can the AI change my accounting data? No by default. Connectors read. A tool that could change data stops and asks you first (Read-only and approvals), and automatic workflow runs are read-only. Which AI should I use? For questions about your data, an agent that can use connectors: Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, or a URL model with tool calling. Ollama is a good private, free helper for Team mode. Try two and compare (AI agents). What does it cost? Raap Nexus itself starts on a free plan (Your plan). The AI you plug in has its own cost, for example an API bill or a subscription. Raap Nexus is built to spend fewer tokens: skills are chosen per question, knowledge is searched instead of sent, saved reports are reused, and Team mode gives each agent only what it needs. How do I save tokens? Ask specific questions with a period and a filter. Switch on only the skills you use, and give each agent only what it needs. Let an agent study your systems once (Knowledge). Keep saved reports on (Saved reports). Use workflow steps that need no AI (\"Call a connector tool\", \"Make a file\"). Can several people use it? Yes. Add users with their own sign-ins and permissions, and share dashboards with a role (Users and permissions). Your plan sets how many. Does it work offline? The app and the help work offline. Agents that call an online model, voice typing, notifications and registration need an internet connection. A local model with a folder or SQLite connector works fully offline. Which languages are available? 18: English, Arabic, Urdu, French, German, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese (Brazil), Russian, Turkish, Hindi, Telugu, Tamil, Malayalam, Indonesian, Chinese (Simplified), Japanese and Korean (Languages and appearance)."},{"id":"glossary","title":"Glossary","summary":"The words used in Raap Nexus and this help.","text":"Word Meaning Agent An AI you plug in: a CLI on your computer or a model by URL and key. CLI A command-line program, here an AI tool such as Claude Code, Codex or Gemini. Connector How the AI reaches a system: an ERP, database, folder or API. Read-only. MCP Model Context Protocol, a standard way for AI tools to call tools and read data. Dashboard A page of widgets, in tabs, that you build by asking the AI. Widget One number, chart, table or map on a dashboard. Skill An instruction pack the assistant loads only when a question needs it. Guardrail A rule an agent must follow, with optional checks on what it writes. Team mode The lead model splits work across several agents in parallel. Workflow Steps that run on a schedule or a trigger. Approval A workflow step where named people must sign off, with a signed record. Knowledge Verified facts the agents learned about your systems, searched when needed. Placeholder A stand-in such as Customer_0001 that replaces a real name when masking is on. Phone mode A secure tunnel that lets your phone reach this computer. Recovery code The code that opens your data on another computer or after a hardware change. Owner The first user, with every permission, always. Techlogica The company that develops Raap Nexus, issues keys and connectors, and delivers updates. Marketplace Where you ask Techlogica for more users, dashboards, products and add-ons. Site and group hub A company location running Raap Nexus, and the hub that shows several sites together."}];